A heating controller turns ON at x<=low, OFF at x>=high, and otherwise retains supplied previous state 0/1. Temperatures are degrees C and low<high. Return next state for one sample. Supplied values: {"high":24,"low":20,"previous":0,"x":19}

Result: 1 state. Apply the two inclusive thresholds first. Inside the dead band, preserve the prior state; this suppresses chatter near one threshold.

