For an ideal continuous-conduction buck, supplied Vin/Vout are V, L is H and switching frequency Hz. Calculate peak-to-peak inductor current A. Ideal duty ratio is Vout/Vin; parasitics and ratings are excluded. Supplied values: {"hz":100000,"l":0.0001,"vin":12,"vout":5}

Result: 0.291666666667 A. During on-time, inductor slope is (Vin-Vout)/L and on-time is (Vout/Vin)/f. Their product is peak-to-peak ripple; off-time must give the same magnitude.

