For an ideal op-amp summing node at 0 V, calculate the output. Rf, R1 and R2 are in ohm; V1 and V2 in V. The supplied output rails are -12 and +12 V. Supplied values: {"r1":20000,"r2":40000,"rf":10000,"v1":2,"v2":4}

Result: -2 V. KCL gives Vout = -Rf*(V1/R1 + V2/R2); the computed voltage must remain within the supplied rails.

